## Faults and scope

Four nonzero diagnostic commands: 5, 7, 8 and 11.
Three were unsuccessful filename/reference searches; command 7 established
that the owned output paths did not yet exist. These are execution/discovery
facts, not mathematical failures. Discovery recovered at command 14.

Content fault: literal 1023b does not specify the extent and timing of the
nonaccelerated remainder. It is retained as source-insufficient, not repaired.
Tasks with more than one valid solution are not execution or content faults.

The final command, number 17, is one bounded existing-Node exact rational
math/structure check plus source binding and generated receipt/freeze writing.
It uses no installed math library and makes no network call. Source rehashing
at freeze binds the final evidence; it is not another solve or comparison.
No repeated mathematical check is authorized or planned.

